  "entry": "code/app.py",
  "notes": "Found in a public repository and run by a computer-use agent (batch public-1). You upload a small CSV or Excel table of bacterial counts. The app removes rows with missing values, works out from the column names whether it is a growth curve, a plate colony count or an antibiotic-vs-control comparison, and then shows the matching statistics, plots and a written summary, which you can download as a TXT or PDF report. Data used in the run: example. tree.json is the workflow the agent did and a second agent replayed; run.json says how.",
